+void FlowSolver::apply_viscous_initial_profile() {
+  / The supplied meshes have very thin first cells at no-slip walls.  Starting
+  / from a uniform freestream would impose an impulsive velocity jump across
+  / one cell and an enormous initial wall shear.  Construct a smooth linear
+  / wall-normal profile instead.  This changes only the t=0 initial condition.
